<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Altdorf, Uri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Altdorf is the capital of the Swiss canton of Uri, near the southern end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-lucerne">Lake Lucerne</a> on the road to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotthard-pass">Gotthard Pass</a>. It is the setting of the legend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-tell">William Tell</a>, who was said to have shot an apple from his son's head in its square. A Tell monument by Richard Kissling has stood there since 1895.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/altdorf-uri.jpg" alt="Altdorf, Uri" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paebi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Altdorf_Ortskern.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
